# A soft FM bell, held rather than struck: two carriers a hair apart at 1.5
# times the note, each with a modulator just over the note, so the partials
# sit at 0.5, 1.5, 2.5, 3.5... times it, a little mistuned, in pairs that beat
# ten times a second. Measured on C#5: level to within 7 dB from 840 Hz to
# 3.1 kHz, 10 dB down at 3.6 kHz, 16 at 4.2 kHz, 24 at 4.7 kHz and gone after.
# The carriers come up over 0.3 s (the first 50 ms are 13 dB under the peak),
# so a note has no edge. The modulators fade faster than the carriers: the
# top dies first. A slow, shallow vibrato keeps a held note from standing
# still.
module fm glass {
  algorithm dual_pairs
  level 2
  mod_index 92%
  vibrato_rate 4.5hz
  vibrato_depth 25%
  op0_ratio 1.5x
  op1_ratio 1.005x
  op2_ratio 1.518x
  op3_ratio 1.005x
  op0_envelope 0.4 2 0.35 1.5
  op1_envelope 0.2 1.8 0.55 1.2
  op2_envelope 0.4 2 0.35 1.5
  op3_envelope 0.2 1.8 0.55 1.2
}
